{"abstract":[{"text":"Enhance your app experience with system-provided and custom Liquid Glass.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/technologies","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI"],["doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/technologies","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View-styles"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass"},"kind":"article","legalNotices":{"copyright":"Copyright &copy; 2026 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.","privacyPolicy":"https:\/\/www.apple.com\/privacy\/privacy-policy","termsOfUse":"https:\/\/www.apple.com\/legal\/internet-services\/terms\/site.html"},"metadata":{"images":[{"identifier":"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-PageImage-card.png","type":"card"}],"modules":[{"name":"SwiftUI"}],"platforms":[{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"26.0","name":"iOS"},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"26.0","name":"iPadOS"},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"26.0","name":"Mac Catalyst"},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"26.0","name":"macOS"},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"26.0","name":"Xcode"}],"role":"sampleCode","roleHeading":"Sample Code","title":"Landmarks: Building an app with Liquid Glass"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Landmarks is a SwiftUI app that demonstrates how to use the new dynamic and expressive design feature, Liquid Glass. The Landmarks app lets people explore interesting sites around the world. Whether it’s a national park near their home or a far-flung location on a different continent, the app provides a way for people to organize and mark their adventures and receive custom activity badges along the way. Landmarks runs on iPad, iPhone, and Mac.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-1","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Landmarks uses a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/NavigationSplitView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to organize and navigate to content in the app, and demonstrates several key concepts to optimize the use of Liquid Glass:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Stretching content behind the sidebar and inspector with the background extension effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Extending horizontal scroll views under a sidebar or inspector.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Leveraging the system-provided glass effect in toolbars.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Applying Liquid Glass effects to custom interface elements and animations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Building a new app icon with Icon Composer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sample also demonstrates several techniques to use when changing window sizes, and for adding global search.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Apply-a-background-extension-effect","level":2,"text":"Apply a background extension effect","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sample applies a background extension effect to the featured landmark header in the top view, and the main image in the landmark detail view. This effect extends and blurs the image under the sidebar and inspector when they’re open, creating a full edge-to-edge experience.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-2","metadata":{"deviceFrame":"iPadPro12-9"},"type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To achieve this effect, the sample creates and configures an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Image","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that extends to both the leading and trailing edges of the containing view, and applies the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/backgroundExtensionEffect()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" modifier to the image. For the featured image, the sample adds an overlay with a headline and button after the modifier, so that only the image extends under the sidebar and inspector.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sample also extends the image beyond the top safe area, and adds logic to interactively extend the image when you scroll down beyond the view’s bounds. While this improves the experience of the image in the app, it isn’t required to implement the background extension effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For more information, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Applying-a-background-extension-effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Extend-horizontal-scrolling-under-the-sidebar","level":2,"text":"Extend horizontal scrolling under the sidebar","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Within each continent section in ","type":"text"},{"code":"LandmarksView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"LandmarkHorizontalListView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shows a horizontally scrolling list of landmark views. When open, the landmark views can scroll underneath the sidebar or inspector.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To achieve this effect, the app aligns the scroll views next to the leading and trailing edges of the containing view.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-3","metadata":{"deviceFrame":"iPadPro12-9"},"type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For more information, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Extending-horizontal-scrolling-under-a-sidebar-or-inspector","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Refine-the-Liquid-Glass-in-the-toolbar","level":2,"text":"Refine the Liquid Glass in the toolbar","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"LandmarkDetailView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the sample adds toolbar items for:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"sharing a landmark","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"adding or removing a landmark from a list of Favorites","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"adding or removing a landmark from Collections","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"showing or hiding the inspector","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The system applies Liquid Glass to toolbar items automatically:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-4","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sample also organizes the toolbar into related groups, instead of having all the buttons in one group. For more information, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Refining-the-system-provided-glass-effect-in-toolbars","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Display-badges-with-Liquid-Glass","level":2,"text":"Display badges with Liquid Glass","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Badges provide people with a visual indicator of the activities they’ve recorded in the Landmarks app. When a person completes all four activities for a landmark, they earn that landmark’s badge. The sample uses custom Liquid Glass elements with badges, and shows how to coordinate animations with Liquid Glass.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-5","metadata":{"deviceFrame":"iPhone14Pro"},"type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To create a custom Liquid Glass badge, Landmarks uses a view with an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Image","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to display a system symbol image for the badge. The badge has a background hexagon ","type":"text"},{"code":"Image","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" filled with a custom color. The badge view uses the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffect(_:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" modifier to apply Liquid Glass to the badge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To demonstrate the morphing effect that the system provides with Liquid Glass animations, the sample organizes the badges and the toggle button into a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/GlassEffectContainer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and assigns each badge a unique ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View\/glassEffectID(_:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For more information, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Displaying-custom-activity-badges","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". For information about building custom views with Liquid Glass, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Applying-Liquid-Glass-to-custom-views","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Create-the-app-icon-with-Icon-Composer","level":2,"text":"Create the app icon with Icon Composer","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Landmarks includes a dynamic and expressive app icon composed in Icon Composer. You build app icons with four layers that the system uses to produce specular highlights when a person moves their device, so that the icon responds as if light was reflecting off the glass. The Settings app allows people to personalize the icon by selecting light, dark, clear, or tinted variants of your app icon as well.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For more information on creating a new app icon, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Xcode\/creating-your-app-icon-using-icon-composer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For design guidance, see Human Interface Guidelines >  ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/app-icons","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sampleCodeDownload":{"action":{"identifier":"a88428e6793e\/LandmarksBuildingAnAppWithLiquidGlass.zip","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"Download","type":"reference"},"kind":"sampleDownload"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/TechnologyOverviews\/adopting-liquid-glass","doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/tutorials\/Develop-in-Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Updates\/SwiftUI"],"title":"Essentials"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"App-features","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Applying-a-background-extension-effect","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Extending-horizontal-scrolling-under-a-sidebar-or-inspector","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Refining-the-system-provided-glass-effect-in-toolbars","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Displaying-custom-activity-badges"],"title":"App features"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftui\/landmarks-building-an-app-with-liquid-glass"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]},{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftui\/landmarks-building-an-app-with-liquid-glass"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"references":{"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-1":{"alt":"An image of screenshots of the landmark detail view for Mount Fuji in the Landmarks app, in a Mac, iPad, and iPhone.","identifier":"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-1","type":"image","variants":[{"traits":["2x","light"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-1@2x.png"},{"traits":["2x","dark"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-1~dark@2x.png"}]},"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-2":{"alt":"An image of the landmark detail view for Mount Fuji in the Landmarks app on an iPad, with the sidebar visible.","identifier":"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-2","type":"image","variants":[{"traits":["2x","light"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-2@2x.png"},{"traits":["2x","dark"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-2~dark@2x.png"}]},"Landmarks-Building-an-app-with-Liquid-Glass-3":{"alt":"An image of the landmarks view on an iPad, with the sidebar visible and some landmarks vi